      ],
      "title": "packet-cql: keys with length -1 are NULL values in BATCH operations",
      "message": "packet-cql: keys with length -1 are NULL values in BATCH operations\n\nWhen procssing BATCH statements, Wireshark did not properly handled keys with length < 0 , which actually means that no value\nis sent on the wire..\nThis fixes it (and as a results, parses properly some result packets it failed to parse properly before).\n\nSigned-off-by: Yaniv Kaul <yaniv.kaul@scylladb.com>\n",
      "author_name": "Yaniv Kaul",
      "author_email": "yaniv.kaul@scylladb.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-01-01T15:24:32.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2023-01-02T12:13:17.000+00:00",
